From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:21:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hk: offer sparse binding and residency on G16G on request

Sparse binding and residency are gated to G17P in four places: the
features, the SSTT flush-invalidate record after a sparse texture table
update, the queue's flush stream, and the buffer residency map. G16G
(T8132, M4) reports the same USC 3 / HAL 200 kernel contract as G17P,
uses the Gen9 texture descriptor whose Sparse mode the image view already
packs, and goes through the same native AGX3 bind and copy paths, so the
gates exclude it only because it was never qualified.

Name the record's chips in agx3_chip_has_sstt_flush() and include G16G
there and in the buffer residency map. Advertise the features on G16G
only when ASAHI_G16G_SPARSE=1, so the default stays off until the sparse
transfers are measured on hardware.

Add vulkan-sparse-transfer, which binds a checkerboard of sparse buffer
chunks and image tiles, copies them back, moves one binding to another
place and copies again, so a translation table the GPU did not see after
the rebind shows as a wrong word.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 src/asahi/genxml/agx3_cmdstream.h             |  15 +-
 src/asahi/vulkan/hk_buffer.c                  |   1 +
 src/asahi/vulkan/hk_physical_device.c         |  10 +-
 src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c                   |   6 +-
 src/asahi/vulkan/meson.build                  |   9 +
 .../vulkan/tests/vulkan_sparse_transfer.c     | 603 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 635 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/asahi/vulkan/tests/vulkan_sparse_transfer.c

diff --git a/src/asahi/genxml/agx3_cmdstream.h b/src/asahi/genxml/agx3_cmdstream.h
index 0f197d9c51a..31c321a8199 100644
--- a/src/asahi/genxml/agx3_cmdstream.h
+++ b/src/asahi/genxml/agx3_cmdstream.h
@@ -750,7 +750,16 @@ agx3_cdm_barrier_unpack(enum agx_chip chip, const void *packed,
 
 /* HAL200 and HAL300 encodeSSTTFlushInvalidate emit this standalone record after the
  * CPU changes a sparse texture translation table. It is not an ordinary CDM
- * barrier: the low control byte and SSTT selector at bit 14 are distinct. */
+ * barrier: the low control byte and SSTT selector at bit 14 are distinct.
+ * G16G (T8132) reports the same USC 3 / HAL 200 kernel contract as G17P, so
+ * it takes the same record. */
+static inline bool
+agx3_chip_has_sstt_flush(enum agx_chip chip)
+{
+   return chip == AGX_CHIP_G17P || chip == AGX_CHIP_G16G ||
+          agx_chip_g17_m5(chip);
+}
+
 static inline bool
 agx3_cdm_sstt_flush_invalidate_pack(
    enum agx_chip chip,
@@ -760,7 +769,7 @@ agx3_cdm_sstt_flush_invalidate_pack(
       return false;
 
    memset(packed, 0, AGX3_CDM_SSTT_FLUSH_INVALIDATE_SIZE);
-   if (chip != AGX_CHIP_G17P && !agx_chip_g17_m5(chip))
+   if (!agx3_chip_has_sstt_flush(chip))
       return false;
 
    agx3_cmdstream_store_le32(packed, UINT32_C(0x60024102));
@@ -772,7 +781,7 @@ agx3_cdm_sstt_flush_invalidate_validate(enum agx_chip chip,
                                         const void *packed,
                                         size_t available)
 {
-   return (chip == AGX_CHIP_G17P || agx_chip_g17_m5(chip)) && packed &&
+   return agx3_chip_has_sstt_flush(chip) && packed &&
           available >= AGX3_CDM_SSTT_FLUSH_INVALIDATE_SIZE &&
           agx3_cmdstream_load_le32((const uint8_t *)packed) ==
              UINT32_C(0x60024102);
